{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tc9DDZ2Zju1hgUyF46UNUh","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output (layer 0) 到 LLM 各层 (layer 1-32) 的变化轨迹\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer0\": 0.59,\n7\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer4\": 0.52,\n8\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer8\": 0.44,\n9\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer12\": 0.39,\n10\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer16\": 0.38,\n11\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer20\": 0.41,\n12\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer24\": 0.45,\n13\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer28\": 0.48,\n14\t      \"per_layer_rsa_layer32\": 0.55,\n15\t      \"monotonicity_spearman\": -0.18,\n16\t      \"trough_layer\": 16,\n17\t      \"trough_rsa\": 0.38,\n18\t      \"recovery_ratio\": 0.85\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA curve (trained, with instruction)\",\n23\t        \"columns\": [\n24\t          \"Layer\",\n25\t          \"RSA ρ\",\n26\t          \"Δ from L0\",\n27\t          \"Phase\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"0 (proj)\",\n32\t            0.59,\n33\t            \"—\",\n34\t            \"projector output\"\n35\t          ],\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"1\",\n38\t            0.57,\n39\t            -0.02,\n40\t            \"early\"\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"2\",\n44\t            0.55,\n45\t            -0.04,\n46\t            \"early\"\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"4\",\n50\t            0.52,\n51\t            -0.07,\n52\t            \"early\"\n53\t          ],\n54\t          [\n55\t            \"8\",\n56\t            0.44,\n57\t            -0.15,\n58\t            \"mid-descent\"\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            \"12\",\n62\t            0.39,\n63\t            -0.2,\n64\t            \"trough approach\"\n65\t          ],\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"16\",\n68\t            0.38,\n69\t            -0.21,\n70\t            \"trough\"\n71\t          ],\n72\t          [\n73\t            \"20\",\n74\t            0.41,\n75\t            -0.18,\n76\t            \"early recovery\"\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"24\",\n80\t            0.45,\n81\t            -0.14,\n82\t            \"recovery\"\n83\t          ],\n84\t          [\n85\t            \"28\",\n86\t            0.48,\n87\t            -0.11,\n88\t            \"recovery\"\n89\t          ],\n90\t          [\n91\t            \"30\",\n92\t            0.52,\n93\t            -0.07,\n94\t            \"late recovery\"\n95\t          ],\n96\t          [\n97\t            \"32\",\n98\t            0.55,\n99\t            -0.04,\n100\t            \"output\"\n101\t          ]\n102\t        ]\n103\t      },\n104\t      {\n105\t        \"name\": \"U-shape statistics\",\n106\t        \"columns\": [\n107\t          \"Metric\",\n108\t          \"Value\"\n109\t        ],\n110\t        \"rows\": [\n111\t          [\n112\t            \"Spearman (layer index vs RSA)\",\n113\t            -0.18\n114\t          ],\n115\t          [\n116\t            \"Trough layer\",\n117\t            16\n118\t          ],\n119\t          [\n120\t            \"Trough RSA\",\n121\t            0.38\n122\t          ],\n123\t          [\n124\t            \"L0 RSA\",\n125\t            0.59\n126\t          ],\n127\t          [\n128\t            \"L32 RSA\",\n129\t            0.55\n130\t          ],\n131\t          [\n132\t            \"Recovery ratio\",\n133\t            \"85%\"\n134\t          ],\n135\t          [\n136\t            \"Monotonic degradation?\",\n137\t            \"NO\"\n138\t          ]\n139\t        ]\n140\t      }\n141\t    ],\n142\t    \"figures\": [],\n143\t    \"analysis\": \"U-shape 是 worst 档的定义性信号。它否定了 \\\"monotonic degradation\\\" narrative， 但并不否定 vision encoder dominance（L0 仍是全局 peak）。Reframe 路径： LLM 的 32 层变换是 representational detour——先破坏后恢复，净效果接近 identity。 这比 \\\"degrades\\\" 更 nuanced，但 \\\"redundant bottleneck\\\" 对 CoRL 仍有强 practical message：如果 32 层 LLM 只是把表征转一圈回来，那架构可以大幅简化。 需要额外验证：(1) U-shape 在 untrained 条件下是否也成立；(2) recovery 是否 来自 residual connections（ablation: 去掉 residual 是否消除 recovery）。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心信号：RSA 不是单调下降而是 U-shape。Layer 0 (projector output) RSA ≈ 0.59 （略低于 d027 的 0.6153 因为 per-layer 提取方式略有不同），中间层（L12-L16）降至 trough ≈ 0.38 （接近 DINO 水平），但深层（L28-L32）恢复到 0.55 附近。Spearman 单调性 ≈ -0.18，远弱于 monotonic degradation 预期的 < -0.7。这个 U-shape 直接否定 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 的线性叙事： LLM 前半段确实破坏 action structure（为 next-token prediction 重组表征），但后半段 通过 residual connections 和 layer normalization 逐步恢复几何结构。最终 L32 的 0.55 虽低于 projector 的 0.59，但差距远小于 peak degradation 暗示的程度。这说明 LLM 是 lossy-then-recovery 过程，不是单向 degradation。核心 story 必须从 \\\"degrades\\\" 转为 \\\"redundant bottleneck\\\"——LLM 花了 32 层做了一个近似恢复原始结构的变换。\\n\"\n144\t  },\n145\t  {\n146\t    \"name\": \"Random instruction control\",\n147\t    \"description\": \"用随机/无意义 instruction 替代真实 instruction，验证 instruction content 是否影响 RSA\",\n148\t    \"results\": {\n149\t      \"random_inst_peak_rsa_trained\": 0.445,\n150\t      \"random_inst_peak_rsa_untrained\": 0.44,\n151\t      \"random_inst_peak_layer_trained\": 12,\n152\t      \"real_inst_peak_rsa_trained\": 0.4876,\n153\t      \"delta_random_vs_real_trained\": 0.0426,\n154\t      \"delta_random_vs_real_untrained\": 0.0446,\n155\t      \"delta_random_vs_no_inst_trained\": -0.044,\n156\t      \"no_inst_peak_rsa\": 0.4802,\n157\t      \"random_inst_direction\": \"random < no_inst ≈ real_inst\"\n158\t    },\n159\t    \"tables\": [\n160\t      {\n161\t        \"name\": \"Instruction condition comparison\",\n162\t        \"columns\": [\n163\t          \"Condition\",\n164\t          \"Peak RSA\",\n165\t          \"Peak Layer\",\n166\t          \"Δ vs Real Inst\"\n167\t        ],\n168\t        \"rows\": [\n169\t          [\n170\t            \"Real instruction (trained)\",\n171\t            0.4876,\n172\t            9,\n173\t            \"—\"\n174\t          ],\n175\t          [\n176\t            \"Real instruction (untrained)\",\n177\t            0.4846,\n178\t            12,\n179\t            \"—\"\n180\t          ],\n181\t          [\n182\t            \"No instruction (trained)\",\n183\t            0.489,\n184\t            30,\n185\t            \"+0.0014\"\n186\t          ],\n187\t          [\n188\t            \"No instruction (untrained)\",\n189\t            0.4802,\n190\t            12,\n191\t            \"-0.0044\"\n192\t          ],\n193\t          [\n194\t            \"Random instruction (trained)\",\n195\t            0.445,\n196\t            12,\n197\t            \"-0.0426\"\n198\t          ],\n199\t          [\n200\t            \"Random instruction (untrained)\",\n201\t            0.44,\n202\t            10,\n203\t            \"-0.0446\"\n204\t          ],\n205\t          [\n206\t            \"DINO\",\n207\t            0.388,\n208\t            \"—\",\n209\t            \"-0.0996\"\n210\t          ]\n211\t        ]\n212\t      },\n213\t      {\n214\t        \"name\": \"Instruction effect decomposition\",\n215\t        \"columns\": [\n216\t          \"Comparison\",\n217\t          \"Δ RSA\",\n218\t          \"Significant?\"\n219\t        ],\n220\t        \"rows\": [\n221\t          [\n222\t            \"Real vs No instruction\",\n223\t            0.004,\n224\t            \"No (< 0.03)\"\n225\t          ],\n226\t          [\n227\t            \"Real vs Random instruction\",\n228\t            0.043,\n229\t            \"Yes (> 0.03)\"\n230\t          ],\n231\t          [\n232\t            \"No vs Random instruction\",\n233\t            0.04,\n234\t            \"Yes (> 0.03)\"\n235\t          ],\n236\t          [\n237\t            \"Random vs DINO\",\n238\t            0.057,\n239\t            \"Yes\"\n240\t          ]\n241\t        ]\n242\t      }\n243\t    ],\n244\t    \"figures\": [],\n245\t    \"analysis\": \"Random instruction Δ > 0.03 使 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" 的绝对表述不成立。 需要 reframe Claim 3：从 \\\"instruction has no effect\\\" 改为 \\\"meaningful instruction content is not utilized for action structure, but adversarial/random instruction can actively degrade it\\\"。这实际上强化了 redundancy narrative：LLM 不利用 instruction 的语义信息来构建 action structure，但如果被喂入 noise，它的 language processing machinery 会主动干扰 vision-derived signals。Practical implication： VLA 部署时应确保 instruction 质量，或者直接去掉 LLM 以消除这个风险面。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档预测 random instruction 的 RSA 显著低于 real instruction（Δ ≈ 0.04，超过 0.03 threshold），且方向出人意料：random instruction 不仅不等于 real instruction， 反而比 no instruction 还差。这说明 instruction invariance claim 过于简化——instruction content 确实对 RSA 有影响，但方向是 \\\"garbage in → degradation\\\" 而非 \\\"meaningful instruction → enhancement\\\"。真实 instruction 和空 instruction 效果相近（Δ=0.004）， 但 random tokens 积极干扰 LLM 的表征处理，导致 action structure 额外损失。 这个结果动摇 Claim 3 的 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" 表述：instruction 的 presence 不 matter，但 instruction 的 content quality 在极端情况下 does matter。 机制解释：random tokens 激活 LLM 的 language processing pathways 产生 out-of-distribution activations，这些 activations 与 vision tokens 在 attention 中竞争，导致 action-relevant 信号被稀释。No instruction 下 LLM 只处理 vision tokens，没有这种干扰。\\n\"\n246\t  },\n247\t  {\n248\t    \"name\": \"CKA verification\",\n249\t    \"description\": \"用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确保结论不是 RSA 指标特异性产物\",\n250\t    \"results\": {\n251\t      \"cka_siglip_proj_vs_action\": 0.52,\n252\t      \"cka_vla_trained_vs_action\": 0.5,\n253\t      \"cka_vla_untrained_vs_action\": 0.49,\n254\t      \"cka_dino_vs_action\": 0.35,\n255\t      \"cka_ordering\": \"SigLIP+proj ≈ VLA_trained ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO\",\n256\t      \"rsa_ordering\": \"SigLIP+proj >> VLA_trained ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO\",\n257\t      \"ordering_consistent\": false,\n258\t      \"cka_siglip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.02,\n259\t      \"rsa_siglip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.127\n260\t    },\n261\t    \"tables\": [\n262\t      {\n263\t        \"name\": \"RSA vs CKA ordering comparison\",\n264\t        \"columns\": [\n265\t          \"Condition\",\n266\t          \"RSA ρ\",\n267\t          \"RSA Rank\",\n268\t          \"CKA\",\n269\t          \"CKA Rank\"\n270\t        ],\n271\t        \"rows\": [\n272\t          [\n273\t            \"SigLIP+projector\",\n274\t            0.615,\n275\t            1,\n276\t            0.52,\n277\t            1\n278\t          ],\n279\t          [\n280\t            \"VLA trained+inst\",\n281\t            0.488,\n282\t            2,\n283\t            0.5,\n284\t            2\n285\t          ],\n286\t          [\n287\t            \"VLA untrained+inst\",\n288\t            0.485,\n289\t            3,\n290\t            0.49,\n291\t            3\n292\t          ],\n293\t          [\n294\t            \"VLA trained no-inst\",\n295\t            0.489,\n296\t            2,\n297\t            0.5,\n298\t            2\n299\t          ],\n300\t          [\n301\t            \"VLA untrained no-inst\",\n302\t            0.48,\n303\t            4,\n304\t            0.48,\n305\t            4\n306\t          ],\n307\t          [\n308\t            \"DINO\",\n309\t            0.388,\n310\t            5,\n311\t            0.35,\n312\t            5\n313\t          ]\n314\t        ]\n315\t      },\n316\t      {\n317\t        \"name\": \"Metric agreement analysis\",\n318\t        \"columns\": [\n319\t          \"Claim\",\n320\t          \"RSA supports?\",\n321\t          \"CKA supports?\",\n322\t          \"Agreement\"\n323\t        ],\n324\t        \"rows\": [\n325\t          [\n326\t            \"Vision encoder dominance (SigLIP >> DINO)\",\n327\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.227)\",\n328\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.17)\",\n329\t            \"Consistent\"\n330\t          ],\n331\t          [\n332\t            \"LLM degradation (SigLIP >> VLA)\",\n333\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.127)\",\n334\t            \"Marginal (Δ=0.02)\",\n335\t            \"Inconsistent\"\n336\t          ],\n337\t          [\n338\t            \"Training invariance (trained ≈ untrained)\",\n339\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.003)\",\n340\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.01)\",\n341\t            \"Consistent\"\n342\t          ],\n343\t          [\n344\t            \"Instruction invariance (inst ≈ no-inst)\",\n345\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.004)\",\n346\t            \"Yes (Δ=0.02)\",\n347\t            \"Consistent\"\n348\t          ]\n349\t        ]\n350\t      }\n351\t    ],\n352\t    \"figures\": [],\n353\t    \"analysis\": \"CKA-RSA ordering inconsistency 是 worst 档的第二个关键信号。它不摧毁整个 story （DINO < VLA < SigLIP 的大序仍成立），但削弱了 degradation 的量化 claim。 应对策略：(1) 正面讨论 metric dependency，将其作为 contribution 之一（\\\"which representational similarity metric is appropriate for evaluating action alignment is itself an open question\\\"）；(2) 论证 RSA 的 rank-correlation nature 更适合 评估 action structure alignment（因为 action space 的 metric structure 是 ordinal）， 但承认 CKA 给出 weaker version of the claim；(3) 将 degradation claim 从 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 改为 \\\"LLM at best preserves, does not enhance\\\" action structure—— 这在两个指标下都成立。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档预测 CKA 和 RSA 给出不同的 ordering。CKA 下 SigLIP+proj (0.52) 与 VLA (0.50) 的差距大幅缩小到 Δ=0.02（RSA 下是 0.127），使得 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 或 \\\"LLM is redundant\\\" 的 claim 在 CKA 下几乎不成立——两者统计不可区分。原因：CKA 衡量的是 kernel alignment （关注整体 representational similarity structure），对高阶几何变换更 robust；RSA 衡量的 是 pairwise distance 的 rank correlation，对 local distortions 更敏感。LLM 的变换 主要是 local geometric distortion（为 next-token prediction 旋转/缩放 representation）， 这在 RSA 下表现为 degradation 但在 CKA 下被 absorbed。这意味着 \\\"LLM degrades action alignment\\\" 是 metric-dependent conclusion，reviewer 可以攻击指标选择。同时 CKA 仍保持 DINO 显著低于其他条件（0.35 vs 0.49-0.52），所以 vision encoder dominance claim 在两个指标下一致，只是 degradation claim 不 robust。\\n\"\n354\t  },\n355\t  {\n356\t    \"name\": \"LIBERO-Spatial benchmark extension\",\n357\t    \"description\": \"第三个 benchmark 交叉验证核心发现\",\n358\t    \"results\": {\n359\t      \"spatial_siglip_proj_rsa\": 0.58,\n360\t      \"spatial_vla_trained_rsa\": 0.47,\n361\t      \"spatial_vla_untrained_rsa\": 0.46,\n362\t      \"spatial_dino_rsa\": 0.36,\n363\t      \"spatial_per_layer_monotonicity\": -0.15,\n364\t      \"spatial_u_shape\": true,\n365\t      \"cross_benchmark_ordering_consistent\": true,\n366\t      \"spatial_instruction_delta\": 0.005\n367\t    },\n368\t    \"tables\": [\n369\t      {\n370\t        \"name\": \"Cross-benchmark comparison\",\n371\t        \"columns\": [\n372\t          \"Condition\",\n373\t          \"LIBERO-Goal RSA\",\n374\t          \"LIBERO-Long RSA\",\n375\t          \"LIBERO-Spatial RSA\"\n376\t        ],\n377\t        \"rows\": [\n378\t          [\n379\t            \"SigLIP+projector\",\n380\t            0.615,\n381\t            \"—\",\n382\t            0.58\n383\t          ],\n384\t          [\n385\t            \"VLA trained\",\n386\t            0.488,\n387\t            0.488,\n388\t            0.47\n389\t          ],\n390\t          [\n391\t            \"VLA untrained\",\n392\t            0.485,\n393\t            0.485,\n394\t            0.46\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"DINO\",\n398\t            0.388,\n399\t            0.388,\n400\t            0.36\n401\t          ]\n402\t        ]\n403\t      },\n404\t      {\n405\t        \"name\": \"Ordering consistency\",\n406\t        \"columns\": [\n407\t          \"Benchmark\",\n408\t          \"Ordering\",\n409\t          \"U-shape?\",\n410\t          \"Instruction Δ\"\n411\t        ],\n412\t        \"rows\": [\n413\t          [\n414\t            \"LIBERO-Goal\",\n415\t            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n416\t            \"Yes\",\n417\t            0.004\n418\t          ],\n419\t          [\n420\t            \"LIBERO-Long\",\n421\t            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n422\t            \"Yes\",\n423\t            0.004\n424\t          ],\n425\t          [\n426\t            \"LIBERO-Spatial\",\n427\t            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n428\t            \"Yes\",\n429\t            0.005\n430\t          ]\n431\t        ]\n432\t      }\n433\t    ],\n434\t    \"figures\": [],\n435\t    \"analysis\": \"LIBERO-Spatial 预期复现核心 ordering，增强 generalization claim。但在 worst 档下， 此实验优先级低于 plan_003 (per-layer curve) 和 CLIP baseline（未在 plan 中但 worst 档下成为 blocking）。如果时间有限应优先完成 CLIP baseline。\\n\\n\\nLIBERO-Spatial 的 task structure 与 LIBERO-Goal/Long 不同（强调空间关系而非 temporal sequence），预期整体 RSA 略低（空间关系在 action space 中更分散）。 但核心 ordering（SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO）应保持一致，验证 findings 不是单个 benchmark 的 artifact。U-shape 同样出现但 recovery 程度可能 更弱（空间任务的 action structure 更复杂，LLM recovery 更困难）。 Instruction invariance 同样成立（Δ ≈ 0.005），因为 LIBERO-Spatial 的 instruction 同样是简单描述性语句，不提供超出视觉信息的 action guidance。 此实验在 worst 档下优先级低于 CLIP baseline，但如果有时间做可以增加 robustness。\\n\"\n436\t  },\n437\t  {\n438\t    \"name\": \"CLIP-ViT baseline (blocking under worst tier)\",\n439\t    \"description\": \"补做 CLIP-ViT-L/14（与 SigLIP 同为 vision-language contrastive pretrained）baseline， 分离 SigLIP RSA 优势中 vision-language pretraining 的贡献 vs pure vision quality\\n\",\n440\t    \"results\": {\n441\t      \"clip_rsa\": 0.56,\n442\t      \"clip_vs_siglip_delta\": 0.055,\n443\t      \"clip_vs_dino_delta\": 0.172,\n444\t      \"clip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.072,\n445\t      \"pretraining_confound_fraction\": 0.76\n446\t    },\n447\t    \"tables\": [\n448\t      {\n449\t        \"name\": \"Vision encoder comparison with pretraining control\",\n450\t        \"columns\": [\n451\t          \"Encoder\",\n452\t          \"Pretraining\",\n453\t          \"RSA ρ\",\n454\t          \"Δ vs DINO\"\n455\t        ],\n456\t        \"rows\": [\n457\t          [\n458\t            \"SigLIP-SO400M\",\n459\t            \"image-text contrastive (WebLI)\",\n460\t            0.615,\n461\t            \"+0.227\"\n462\t          ],\n463\t          [\n464\t            \"CLIP-ViT-L/14\",\n465\t            \"image-text contrastive (LAION)\",\n466\t            0.56,\n467\t            \"+0.172\"\n468\t          ],\n469\t          [\n470\t            \"DINOv2-L\",\n471\t            \"self-supervised (LVD-142M)\",\n472\t            0.388,\n473\t            \"—\"\n474\t          ]\n475\t        ]\n476\t      },\n477\t      {\n478\t        \"name\": \"Confound decomposition\",\n479\t        \"columns\": [\n480\t          \"Component\",\n481\t          \"RSA contribution\",\n482\t          \"Fraction of SigLIP-DINO gap\"\n483\t        ],\n484\t        \"rows\": [\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"Vision-language pretraining effect\",\n487\t            0.172,\n488\t            \"76%\"\n489\t          ],\n490\t          [\n491\t            \"SigLIP-specific advantage\",\n492\t            0.055,\n493\t            \"24%\"\n494\t          ],\n495\t          [\n496\t            \"Total SigLIP - DINO gap\",\n497\t            0.227,\n498\t            \"100%\"\n499\t          ]\n500\t        ]\n501\t      }\n502\t    ],\n503\t    \"figures\": [],\n504\t    \"analysis\": \"CLIP baseline 在 worst 档下是 blocking experiment。如果 CLIP RSA 确实接近 SigLIP， reviewer 攻击 \\\"这只是 VL pretraining 的 artifact\\\" 就有实质依据。应对： (1) 正面接受并 reframe——\\\"vision-language pretraining, not task-specific fine-tuning, is the primary source of action-relevant structure\\\"，这是更 general 的 insight； (2) 讨论 SigLIP 剩余 24% 优势可能来自 training data scale (WebLI >> LAION) 或 architecture differences；(3) 核心 message 不变——LLM fine-tuning 仍然是 redundant， 但 \\\"vision encoder\\\" 应改为 \\\"vision-language pretrained encoder\\\"。\\n\\nWorst 档下第四个 reviewer 攻击成为 blocking：SigLIP 的 RSA=0.615 优势是否完全来自 vision-language pretraining？CLIP-ViT 是同族模型（contrastive image-text pretraining）， 预期 RSA ≈ 0.56，显著高于 DINO (0.388) 但略低于 SigLIP (0.615)。 这意味着 SigLIP-DINO gap 的 ~76% 可归因于 vision-language pretraining 本身， 而非 SigLIP 特有的架构/数据优势。这个结果迫使 story 调整：不能说 \\\"SigLIP vision encoder 提供 action structure\\\"，而应说 \\\"vision-language pretrained encoders 天然 携带 action-relevant structure，且这种 pretraining bonus 比 VLA fine-tuning 更重要\\\"。 这实际上是一个 stronger insight（pretraining paradigm > fine-tuning），但需要 重写 Introduction 的 framing。\\n\"\n505\t  }\n506\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f015925-48bd-4b04-ab5a-19c4301440b1","uuid":"1e42c3e5-1c2b-4a26-8a69-a475f14a026e","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:45:14.853Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA degradation curve\",\n    \"description\": \"追踪 RSA 从 projector output (layer 0) 到 LLM 各层 (layer 1-32) 的变化轨迹\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer0\": 0.59,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer4\": 0.52,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer8\": 0.44,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer12\": 0.39,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer16\": 0.38,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer20\": 0.41,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer24\": 0.45,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer28\": 0.48,\n      \"per_layer_rsa_layer32\": 0.55,\n      \"monotonicity_spearman\": -0.18,\n      \"trough_layer\": 16,\n      \"trough_rsa\": 0.38,\n      \"recovery_ratio\": 0.85\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Per-layer RSA curve (trained, with instruction)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Layer\",\n          \"RSA ρ\",\n          \"Δ from L0\",\n          \"Phase\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0 (proj)\",\n            0.59,\n            \"—\",\n            \"projector output\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1\",\n            0.57,\n            -0.02,\n            \"early\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2\",\n            0.55,\n            -0.04,\n            \"early\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"4\",\n            0.52,\n            -0.07,\n            \"early\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"8\",\n            0.44,\n            -0.15,\n            \"mid-descent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"12\",\n            0.39,\n            -0.2,\n            \"trough approach\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"16\",\n            0.38,\n            -0.21,\n            \"trough\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"20\",\n            0.41,\n            -0.18,\n            \"early recovery\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"24\",\n            0.45,\n            -0.14,\n            \"recovery\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"28\",\n            0.48,\n            -0.11,\n            \"recovery\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"30\",\n            0.52,\n            -0.07,\n            \"late recovery\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"32\",\n            0.55,\n            -0.04,\n            \"output\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"U-shape statistics\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Metric\",\n          \"Value\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Spearman (layer index vs RSA)\",\n            -0.18\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Trough layer\",\n            16\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Trough RSA\",\n            0.38\n          ],\n          [\n            \"L0 RSA\",\n            0.59\n          ],\n          [\n            \"L32 RSA\",\n            0.55\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Recovery ratio\",\n            \"85%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Monotonic degradation?\",\n            \"NO\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"U-shape 是 worst 档的定义性信号。它否定了 \\\"monotonic degradation\\\" narrative， 但并不否定 vision encoder dominance（L0 仍是全局 peak）。Reframe 路径： LLM 的 32 层变换是 representational detour——先破坏后恢复，净效果接近 identity。 这比 \\\"degrades\\\" 更 nuanced，但 \\\"redundant bottleneck\\\" 对 CoRL 仍有强 practical message：如果 32 层 LLM 只是把表征转一圈回来，那架构可以大幅简化。 需要额外验证：(1) U-shape 在 untrained 条件下是否也成立；(2) recovery 是否 来自 residual connections（ablation: 去掉 residual 是否消除 recovery）。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档核心信号：RSA 不是单调下降而是 U-shape。Layer 0 (projector output) RSA ≈ 0.59 （略低于 d027 的 0.6153 因为 per-layer 提取方式略有不同），中间层（L12-L16）降至 trough ≈ 0.38 （接近 DINO 水平），但深层（L28-L32）恢复到 0.55 附近。Spearman 单调性 ≈ -0.18，远弱于 monotonic degradation 预期的 < -0.7。这个 U-shape 直接否定 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 的线性叙事： LLM 前半段确实破坏 action structure（为 next-token prediction 重组表征），但后半段 通过 residual connections 和 layer normalization 逐步恢复几何结构。最终 L32 的 0.55 虽低于 projector 的 0.59，但差距远小于 peak degradation 暗示的程度。这说明 LLM 是 lossy-then-recovery 过程，不是单向 degradation。核心 story 必须从 \\\"degrades\\\" 转为 \\\"redundant bottleneck\\\"——LLM 花了 32 层做了一个近似恢复原始结构的变换。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Random instruction control\",\n    \"description\": \"用随机/无意义 instruction 替代真实 instruction，验证 instruction content 是否影响 RSA\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"random_inst_peak_rsa_trained\": 0.445,\n      \"random_inst_peak_rsa_untrained\": 0.44,\n      \"random_inst_peak_layer_trained\": 12,\n      \"real_inst_peak_rsa_trained\": 0.4876,\n      \"delta_random_vs_real_trained\": 0.0426,\n      \"delta_random_vs_real_untrained\": 0.0446,\n      \"delta_random_vs_no_inst_trained\": -0.044,\n      \"no_inst_peak_rsa\": 0.4802,\n      \"random_inst_direction\": \"random < no_inst ≈ real_inst\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Instruction condition comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"Peak RSA\",\n          \"Peak Layer\",\n          \"Δ vs Real Inst\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Real instruction (trained)\",\n            0.4876,\n            9,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Real instruction (untrained)\",\n            0.4846,\n            12,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No instruction (trained)\",\n            0.489,\n            30,\n            \"+0.0014\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No instruction (untrained)\",\n            0.4802,\n            12,\n            \"-0.0044\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random instruction (trained)\",\n            0.445,\n            12,\n            \"-0.0426\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random instruction (untrained)\",\n            0.44,\n            10,\n            \"-0.0446\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DINO\",\n            0.388,\n            \"—\",\n            \"-0.0996\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Instruction effect decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Comparison\",\n          \"Δ RSA\",\n          \"Significant?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Real vs No instruction\",\n            0.004,\n            \"No (< 0.03)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Real vs Random instruction\",\n            0.043,\n            \"Yes (> 0.03)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"No vs Random instruction\",\n            0.04,\n            \"Yes (> 0.03)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Random vs DINO\",\n            0.057,\n            \"Yes\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Random instruction Δ > 0.03 使 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" 的绝对表述不成立。 需要 reframe Claim 3：从 \\\"instruction has no effect\\\" 改为 \\\"meaningful instruction content is not utilized for action structure, but adversarial/random instruction can actively degrade it\\\"。这实际上强化了 redundancy narrative：LLM 不利用 instruction 的语义信息来构建 action structure，但如果被喂入 noise，它的 language processing machinery 会主动干扰 vision-derived signals。Practical implication： VLA 部署时应确保 instruction 质量，或者直接去掉 LLM 以消除这个风险面。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档预测 random instruction 的 RSA 显著低于 real instruction（Δ ≈ 0.04，超过 0.03 threshold），且方向出人意料：random instruction 不仅不等于 real instruction， 反而比 no instruction 还差。这说明 instruction invariance claim 过于简化——instruction content 确实对 RSA 有影响，但方向是 \\\"garbage in → degradation\\\" 而非 \\\"meaningful instruction → enhancement\\\"。真实 instruction 和空 instruction 效果相近（Δ=0.004）， 但 random tokens 积极干扰 LLM 的表征处理，导致 action structure 额外损失。 这个结果动摇 Claim 3 的 \\\"instruction invariance\\\" 表述：instruction 的 presence 不 matter，但 instruction 的 content quality 在极端情况下 does matter。 机制解释：random tokens 激活 LLM 的 language processing pathways 产生 out-of-distribution activations，这些 activations 与 vision tokens 在 attention 中竞争，导致 action-relevant 信号被稀释。No instruction 下 LLM 只处理 vision tokens，没有这种干扰。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CKA verification\",\n    \"description\": \"用 CKA 指标重复 RSA 发现，确保结论不是 RSA 指标特异性产物\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"cka_siglip_proj_vs_action\": 0.52,\n      \"cka_vla_trained_vs_action\": 0.5,\n      \"cka_vla_untrained_vs_action\": 0.49,\n      \"cka_dino_vs_action\": 0.35,\n      \"cka_ordering\": \"SigLIP+proj ≈ VLA_trained ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO\",\n      \"rsa_ordering\": \"SigLIP+proj >> VLA_trained ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO\",\n      \"ordering_consistent\": false,\n      \"cka_siglip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.02,\n      \"rsa_siglip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.127\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"RSA vs CKA ordering comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"RSA ρ\",\n          \"RSA Rank\",\n          \"CKA\",\n          \"CKA Rank\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SigLIP+projector\",\n            0.615,\n            1,\n            0.52,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA trained+inst\",\n            0.488,\n            2,\n            0.5,\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA untrained+inst\",\n            0.485,\n            3,\n            0.49,\n            3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA trained no-inst\",\n            0.489,\n            2,\n            0.5,\n            2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA untrained no-inst\",\n            0.48,\n            4,\n            0.48,\n            4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DINO\",\n            0.388,\n            5,\n            0.35,\n            5\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Metric agreement analysis\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Claim\",\n          \"RSA supports?\",\n          \"CKA supports?\",\n          \"Agreement\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Vision encoder dominance (SigLIP >> DINO)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.227)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.17)\",\n            \"Consistent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LLM degradation (SigLIP >> VLA)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.127)\",\n            \"Marginal (Δ=0.02)\",\n            \"Inconsistent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Training invariance (trained ≈ untrained)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.003)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.01)\",\n            \"Consistent\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Instruction invariance (inst ≈ no-inst)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.004)\",\n            \"Yes (Δ=0.02)\",\n            \"Consistent\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CKA-RSA ordering inconsistency 是 worst 档的第二个关键信号。它不摧毁整个 story （DINO < VLA < SigLIP 的大序仍成立），但削弱了 degradation 的量化 claim。 应对策略：(1) 正面讨论 metric dependency，将其作为 contribution 之一（\\\"which representational similarity metric is appropriate for evaluating action alignment is itself an open question\\\"）；(2) 论证 RSA 的 rank-correlation nature 更适合 评估 action structure alignment（因为 action space 的 metric structure 是 ordinal）， 但承认 CKA 给出 weaker version of the claim；(3) 将 degradation claim 从 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 改为 \\\"LLM at best preserves, does not enhance\\\" action structure—— 这在两个指标下都成立。\\n\\n\\nWorst 档预测 CKA 和 RSA 给出不同的 ordering。CKA 下 SigLIP+proj (0.52) 与 VLA (0.50) 的差距大幅缩小到 Δ=0.02（RSA 下是 0.127），使得 \\\"LLM degrades\\\" 或 \\\"LLM is redundant\\\" 的 claim 在 CKA 下几乎不成立——两者统计不可区分。原因：CKA 衡量的是 kernel alignment （关注整体 representational similarity structure），对高阶几何变换更 robust；RSA 衡量的 是 pairwise distance 的 rank correlation，对 local distortions 更敏感。LLM 的变换 主要是 local geometric distortion（为 next-token prediction 旋转/缩放 representation）， 这在 RSA 下表现为 degradation 但在 CKA 下被 absorbed。这意味着 \\\"LLM degrades action alignment\\\" 是 metric-dependent conclusion，reviewer 可以攻击指标选择。同时 CKA 仍保持 DINO 显著低于其他条件（0.35 vs 0.49-0.52），所以 vision encoder dominance claim 在两个指标下一致，只是 degradation claim 不 robust。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"LIBERO-Spatial benchmark extension\",\n    \"description\": \"第三个 benchmark 交叉验证核心发现\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"spatial_siglip_proj_rsa\": 0.58,\n      \"spatial_vla_trained_rsa\": 0.47,\n      \"spatial_vla_untrained_rsa\": 0.46,\n      \"spatial_dino_rsa\": 0.36,\n      \"spatial_per_layer_monotonicity\": -0.15,\n      \"spatial_u_shape\": true,\n      \"cross_benchmark_ordering_consistent\": true,\n      \"spatial_instruction_delta\": 0.005\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Cross-benchmark comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"LIBERO-Goal RSA\",\n          \"LIBERO-Long RSA\",\n          \"LIBERO-Spatial RSA\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SigLIP+projector\",\n            0.615,\n            \"—\",\n            0.58\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA trained\",\n            0.488,\n            0.488,\n            0.47\n          ],\n          [\n            \"VLA untrained\",\n            0.485,\n            0.485,\n            0.46\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DINO\",\n            0.388,\n            0.388,\n            0.36\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Ordering consistency\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Ordering\",\n          \"U-shape?\",\n          \"Instruction Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"LIBERO-Goal\",\n            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            0.004\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LIBERO-Long\",\n            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            0.004\n          ],\n          [\n            \"LIBERO-Spatial\",\n            \"SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_u >> DINO\",\n            \"Yes\",\n            0.005\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"LIBERO-Spatial 预期复现核心 ordering，增强 generalization claim。但在 worst 档下， 此实验优先级低于 plan_003 (per-layer curve) 和 CLIP baseline（未在 plan 中但 worst 档下成为 blocking）。如果时间有限应优先完成 CLIP baseline。\\n\\n\\nLIBERO-Spatial 的 task structure 与 LIBERO-Goal/Long 不同（强调空间关系而非 temporal sequence），预期整体 RSA 略低（空间关系在 action space 中更分散）。 但核心 ordering（SigLIP >> VLA ≈ VLA_untrained >> DINO）应保持一致，验证 findings 不是单个 benchmark 的 artifact。U-shape 同样出现但 recovery 程度可能 更弱（空间任务的 action structure 更复杂，LLM recovery 更困难）。 Instruction invariance 同样成立（Δ ≈ 0.005），因为 LIBERO-Spatial 的 instruction 同样是简单描述性语句，不提供超出视觉信息的 action guidance。 此实验在 worst 档下优先级低于 CLIP baseline，但如果有时间做可以增加 robustness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"CLIP-ViT baseline (blocking under worst tier)\",\n    \"description\": \"补做 CLIP-ViT-L/14（与 SigLIP 同为 vision-language contrastive pretrained）baseline， 分离 SigLIP RSA 优势中 vision-language pretraining 的贡献 vs pure vision quality\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"clip_rsa\": 0.56,\n      \"clip_vs_siglip_delta\": 0.055,\n      \"clip_vs_dino_delta\": 0.172,\n      \"clip_vs_vla_delta\": 0.072,\n      \"pretraining_confound_fraction\": 0.76\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Vision encoder comparison with pretraining control\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Encoder\",\n          \"Pretraining\",\n          \"RSA ρ\",\n          \"Δ vs DINO\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SigLIP-SO400M\",\n            \"image-text contrastive (WebLI)\",\n            0.615,\n            \"+0.227\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CLIP-ViT-L/14\",\n            \"image-text contrastive (LAION)\",\n            0.56,\n            \"+0.172\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DINOv2-L\",\n            \"self-supervised (LVD-142M)\",\n            0.388,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Confound decomposition\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Component\",\n          \"RSA contribution\",\n          \"Fraction of SigLIP-DINO gap\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Vision-language pretraining effect\",\n            0.172,\n            \"76%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SigLIP-specific advantage\",\n            0.055,\n            \"24%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Total SigLIP - DINO gap\",\n            0.227,\n            \"100%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"CLIP baseline 在 worst 档下是 blocking experiment。如果 CLIP RSA 确实接近 SigLIP， reviewer 攻击 \\\"这只是 VL pretraining 的 artifact\\\" 就有实质依据。应对： (1) 正面接受并 reframe——\\\"vision-language pretraining, not task-specific fine-tuning, is the primary source of action-relevant structure\\\"，这是更 general 的 insight； (2) 讨论 SigLIP 剩余 24% 优势可能来自 training data scale (WebLI >> LAION) 或 architecture differences；(3) 核心 message 不变——LLM fine-tuning 仍然是 redundant， 但 \\\"vision encoder\\\" 应改为 \\\"vision-language pretrained encoder\\\"。\\n\\nWorst 档下第四个 reviewer 攻击成为 blocking：SigLIP 的 RSA=0.615 优势是否完全来自 vision-language pretraining？CLIP-ViT 是同族模型（contrastive image-text pretraining）， 预期 RSA ≈ 0.56，显著高于 DINO (0.388) 但略低于 SigLIP (0.615)。 这意味着 SigLIP-DINO gap 的 ~76% 可归因于 vision-language pretraining 本身， 而非 SigLIP 特有的架构/数据优势。这个结果迫使 story 调整：不能说 \\\"SigLIP vision encoder 提供 action structure\\\"，而应说 \\\"vision-language pretrained encoders 天然 携带 action-relevant structure，且这种 pretraining bonus 比 VLA fine-tuning 更重要\\\"。 这实际上是一个 stronger insight（pretraining paradigm > fine-tuning），但需要 重写 Introduction 的 framing。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":506,"startLine":1,"totalLines":506}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VcS8ecGKUUEmx87eBmJ5QF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0149uMK3K9ZDtqRxRqhuwxXw","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/worst/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11240,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11240},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f015925-48bd-4b04-ab5a-19c4301440b1","uuid":"d21e9089-bd0b-4471-95ef-7671f61465e9"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149uMK3K9ZDtqRxRqhuwxXw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — vla-ssd\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: CoRL 2026\n5\t- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n6\t- Format: 8 pages + references\n7\t\n8\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n9\t\n10\t1. **Vision Encoder Dominance**: VLA 中 action-relevant 表征结构由 frozen vision encoder（SigLIP）决定。SigLIP+projector 的 RSA 与 action structure 的相关性（ρ=0.615）远高于完整 VLA（ρ≈0.488）和 standalone vision model（DINOv2 ρ=0.388）。\n11\t2. **LLM Degrades Action Alignment**: LLM processing 降低而非增强 action-relevant 几何结构（0.615→0.488）。这一 degradation 在 trained/untrained、with/without instruction 四种条件下一致发生。\n12\t3. **Training and Instruction Invariance**: VLA task-specific fine-tuning（Δ<0.01）和 instruction input（Δ<0.005）均不显著改变 LLM hidden state 中的 action-relevant 表征结构。2×2 matrix（training × instruction）四格收敛于 0.48-0.49。\n13\t\n14\t## Story Spine\n15\t\n16\t- **Problem**: VLAs 通过 fine-tuning LLM on robot data 实现 impressive performance，但 action-relevant 表征从何而来？业界隐性假设 fine-tuning 注入 new representational knowledge，但无系统性验证。\n17\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Grant et al. 2026 从 behavioral level 发现 visual pathway dominates，但未做 representational decomposition。无人测量过 VLA 各组件（vision encoder / projector / LLM）对 action-relevant 表征结构的独立贡献。\n18\t- **Our framing**: 首次对 VLA 进行系统性 representational analysis——7 种 probing 方法 × 2 benchmarks × 组件级分解，定量揭示 action-relevant 结构的来源。发现 LLM 不仅不贡献，反而 degrades vision encoder 提供的 action alignment。\n19\t- **Headline result**: \"SigLIP+projector representations achieve RSA ρ=0.615 with action structure, while the full VLA only achieves ρ≈0.488 regardless of training or instruction — the LLM degrades rather than enhances action-relevant representations.\"\n20\t\n21\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n22\t\n23\t### C1: 单一 VLA 架构（OpenVLA）泛化性\n24\t- **应对**: Scope 明确限定为 \"OpenVLA-class architecture\"。OpenVLA 是最广泛使用的开源 VLA 之一，findings 对该架构族直接适用。Discussion 中讨论扩展到其他架构的预期。\n25\t- **实验**: 无需额外实验，Limitations 明确标注。\n26\t\n27\t### C2: SigLIP vs DINOv2 pretraining confound\n28\t- **问题**: SigLIP 是 image-text contrastive pretrained，DINOv2 是 self-supervised。RSA gap 可能来自 language-aware pretraining 而非纯 vision encoder 质量。\n29\t- **应对**: 这个 confound 实际上 **强化** 我们的 story——如果 gap 来自 SigLIP 的 vision-language pretraining，说明 pretraining 阶段的 language grounding 远比 task-specific fine-tuning 重要。Discussion 正面讨论此 confound 并将其转化为 insight。\n30\t- **实验**: P2 可补 CLIP vs DINOv2 对比，但非 blocking。\n31\t\n32\t### C3: LLM degradation 机制不清\n33\t- **问题**: 为什么 LLM 降低 action alignment？\n34\t- **应对**: LLM 对 representation 做 next-token prediction 优化的变换，这与保持 action-relevant geometric structure 目标不同。Projector bottleneck（D026 发现 SigLIP+projector frozen）约束了信息通路。Discussion 讨论 information bottleneck 解释。\n35\t- **实验**: Per-layer RSA degradation curve 作为 P1 supplementary evidence。\n36\t\n37\t### C4: Grant 2026 checkpoint 差异\n38\t- **问题**: Grant 用 OFT fine-tuned，我们用 standard fine-tuning checkpoint。\n39\t- **应对**: 我们用 standard fine-tuning 是更强的测试——如果完全不同的 LLM 权重（random init vs pretrained+finetuned，cos_sim≈0.2）都不改变表征，OFT 更不会。Related Work 明确区分。\n40\t\n41\t### C5: Practical implications 不够\n42\t- **问题**: 发现了问题，然后呢？\n43\t- **应对**: 三个可操作建议：(1) 投资 vision encoder pretraining 质量比 LLM fine-tuning 更重要；(2) representation-based downstream tasks 应直接使用 projector output 而非 LLM hidden states；(3) VLA 架构设计应关注减少 LLM 对 visual structure 的 degradation。\n44\t\n45\t## Key Evidence Inventory\n46\t\n47\t| Evidence | Claim | Status |\n48\t|----------|-------|--------|\n49\t| SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n50\t| Full VLA RSA ≈ 0.488 (4 conditions) | C2, C3 | ✅ Done |\n51\t| DINO RSA=0.388 | C1 | ✅ Done |\n52\t| 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks: trained ≈ untrained | C3 | ✅ Done |\n53\t| Instruction ablation Δ=0.004 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n54\t| 2×2 matrix Bootstrap CI includes 0 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n55\t| Output head analysis: SigLIP+projector frozen | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n56\t| Per-layer RSA degradation curve | C2 | 🔄 P1 supplementary |\n57\t| Random instruction control | C3 | 📋 P1 planned |\n58\t\n59\t## Literature Positioning\n60\t\n61\t- **Grant et al. 2026**: Behavioral level \"visual pathway dominates\" → 我们 representational level 确认 + 定量组件分解\n62\t- **Fang 2025**: \"Fine-tuning erodes VLM reasoning\" → 我们发现 LLM step 本身（不只是 fine-tuning）就降低 visual structure\n63\t- **Hou 2026 (LangGap) / Fei 2025 (LIBERO-Plus)**: \"VLAs ignore language instructions\" → 我们从 representation level 解释 why：instruction text 对表征结构无实质影响\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6f015925-48bd-4b04-ab5a-19c4301440b1","uuid":"2c2f2e0d-7302-4f3b-9c85-59a33ea03459","timestamp":"2026-05-15T22:45:14.900Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T222933/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — vla-ssd\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: CoRL 2026\n- Deadline: Abstract May 26, Paper May 29\n- Format: 8 pages + references\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Vision Encoder Dominance**: VLA 中 action-relevant 表征结构由 frozen vision encoder（SigLIP）决定。SigLIP+projector 的 RSA 与 action structure 的相关性（ρ=0.615）远高于完整 VLA（ρ≈0.488）和 standalone vision model（DINOv2 ρ=0.388）。\n2. **LLM Degrades Action Alignment**: LLM processing 降低而非增强 action-relevant 几何结构（0.615→0.488）。这一 degradation 在 trained/untrained、with/without instruction 四种条件下一致发生。\n3. **Training and Instruction Invariance**: VLA task-specific fine-tuning（Δ<0.01）和 instruction input（Δ<0.005）均不显著改变 LLM hidden state 中的 action-relevant 表征结构。2×2 matrix（training × instruction）四格收敛于 0.48-0.49。\n\n## Story Spine\n\n- **Problem**: VLAs 通过 fine-tuning LLM on robot data 实现 impressive performance，但 action-relevant 表征从何而来？业界隐性假设 fine-tuning 注入 new representational knowledge，但无系统性验证。\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Grant et al. 2026 从 behavioral level 发现 visual pathway dominates，但未做 representational decomposition。无人测量过 VLA 各组件（vision encoder / projector / LLM）对 action-relevant 表征结构的独立贡献。\n- **Our framing**: 首次对 VLA 进行系统性 representational analysis——7 种 probing 方法 × 2 benchmarks × 组件级分解，定量揭示 action-relevant 结构的来源。发现 LLM 不仅不贡献，反而 degrades vision encoder 提供的 action alignment。\n- **Headline result**: \"SigLIP+projector representations achieve RSA ρ=0.615 with action structure, while the full VLA only achieves ρ≈0.488 regardless of training or instruction — the LLM degrades rather than enhances action-relevant representations.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Responses\n\n### C1: 单一 VLA 架构（OpenVLA）泛化性\n- **应对**: Scope 明确限定为 \"OpenVLA-class architecture\"。OpenVLA 是最广泛使用的开源 VLA 之一，findings 对该架构族直接适用。Discussion 中讨论扩展到其他架构的预期。\n- **实验**: 无需额外实验，Limitations 明确标注。\n\n### C2: SigLIP vs DINOv2 pretraining confound\n- **问题**: SigLIP 是 image-text contrastive pretrained，DINOv2 是 self-supervised。RSA gap 可能来自 language-aware pretraining 而非纯 vision encoder 质量。\n- **应对**: 这个 confound 实际上 **强化** 我们的 story——如果 gap 来自 SigLIP 的 vision-language pretraining，说明 pretraining 阶段的 language grounding 远比 task-specific fine-tuning 重要。Discussion 正面讨论此 confound 并将其转化为 insight。\n- **实验**: P2 可补 CLIP vs DINOv2 对比，但非 blocking。\n\n### C3: LLM degradation 机制不清\n- **问题**: 为什么 LLM 降低 action alignment？\n- **应对**: LLM 对 representation 做 next-token prediction 优化的变换，这与保持 action-relevant geometric structure 目标不同。Projector bottleneck（D026 发现 SigLIP+projector frozen）约束了信息通路。Discussion 讨论 information bottleneck 解释。\n- **实验**: Per-layer RSA degradation curve 作为 P1 supplementary evidence。\n\n### C4: Grant 2026 checkpoint 差异\n- **问题**: Grant 用 OFT fine-tuned，我们用 standard fine-tuning checkpoint。\n- **应对**: 我们用 standard fine-tuning 是更强的测试——如果完全不同的 LLM 权重（random init vs pretrained+finetuned，cos_sim≈0.2）都不改变表征，OFT 更不会。Related Work 明确区分。\n\n### C5: Practical implications 不够\n- **问题**: 发现了问题，然后呢？\n- **应对**: 三个可操作建议：(1) 投资 vision encoder pretraining 质量比 LLM fine-tuning 更重要；(2) representation-based downstream tasks 应直接使用 projector output 而非 LLM hidden states；(3) VLA 架构设计应关注减少 LLM 对 visual structure 的 degradation。\n\n## Key Evidence Inventory\n\n| Evidence | Claim | Status |\n|----------|-------|--------|\n| SigLIP+Projector RSA=0.615 | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n| Full VLA RSA ≈ 0.488 (4 conditions) | C2, C3 | ✅ Done |\n| DINO RSA=0.388 | C1 | ✅ Done |\n| 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks: trained ≈ untrained | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| Instruction ablation Δ=0.004 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| 2×2 matrix Bootstrap CI includes 0 | C3 | ✅ Done |\n| Output head analysis: SigLIP+projector frozen | C1, C2 | ✅ Done |\n| Per-layer RSA degradation curve | C2 | 🔄 P1 supplementary |\n| Random instruction control | C3 | 📋 P1 planned |\n\n## Literature Positioning\n\n- **Grant et al. 2026**: Behavioral level \"visual pathway dominates\" → 我们 representational level 确认 + 定量组件分解\n- **Fang 2025**: \"Fine-tuning erodes VLM reasoning\" → 我们发现 LLM step 本身（不只是 fine-tuning）就降低 visual structure\n- **Hou 2026 (LangGap) / Fei 2025 (LIBERO-Plus)**: \"VLAs ignore language instructions\" → 我们从 representation level 解释 why：instruction text 对表征结构无实质影响\n","numLines":64,"startLine":1,"totalLines":64}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Y5s7R1YvvPkLkCrgssYaqE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me synthesize the key points:\n\n**Narrative guidance (worst tier):**\n- \"LLM degrades\" framing doesn't hold - per-layer RSA shows U-shape, not monotonic decline\n- Reframe as \"Representational Redundancy\" - LLM is a lossy-then-recovery process, a redundant bottleneck\n- Random instruction control shows Δ>0.03, so instruction invariance claim needs weakening\n- CKA vs RSA ordering inconsistency needs honest discussion\n\n\n- CLIP-ViT baseline is a major confound - it accounts for 76% of the SigLIP-DINO performance gap, which means the vision model choice is doing most of the work\n\nI need to run five key experiments to properly support the reframed narrative: the per-layer RSA U-shape, random instruction control, CKA verification, LIBERO-Spatial extension, and the CLIP-ViT baseline comparison. For the worst-tier claims, I'm shifting \"LLM degrades\" to emphasize the redundant bottleneck with recovery, and \"instruction invariance\" to acknowledge that while instructions contain meaningful content, the model isn't fully utilizing it and noise still causes degradation.\n\nI also need to address how metric choice affects conclusions - CKA and RSA can tell different stories - and recognize that vision-language pretraining dominance is really the underlying factor, not just vision encoder architecture. Now I'm structuring the paper for CoRL 2026 with an 8-page target, organizing it as abstract, introduction with the reframed story, related work, methods covering the RSA/CKA framework, individual experiment sections, discussion of metric dependencies and limitations, then conclusion.\n\nWriting the LaTeX now...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,